Package: hranix-shield
Version: 0.1.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: systemd, libc6
Maintainer: Hranix <security@hranix.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/hranix/ai-assistant
Description: Hranix Shield — free open-source security panel (Phase 0)
 Native Linux install of Hranix Shield's Phase 0 "Панель безопасности" —
 the security-facing panel of the Hranix Assistant platform, licensed
 AGPLv3+CLA. Runs as a systemd system service under a dedicated
 unprivileged user (hranix-shield), serving a local web panel on
 127.0.0.1:8080. Optional companion services (CrowdSec, ClamAV, Wazuh
 Manager) are separate Docker containers, not part of this package — see
 infra/security/*/docker-compose.yml in the source repository.
 .
 This native install exists specifically so the "Периметр" (host firewall /
 disk encryption) and "Сеть" (osquery) security consoles can inspect the
 REAL host OS — a Docker deployment of the same panel can only ever see the
 Linux container it runs in, never the actual host, regardless of the
 host's own OS.
 .
 A-25: this package's postinst also installs and enrolls the official
 Wazuh AGENT (GPLv2, from Wazuh's own apt repository — a separate systemd
 service, never linked into this package's own AGPLv3+CLA code) against
 the Wazuh Manager container above, so the "Журналы ОС" console's file-
 integrity monitoring watches this host's real files instead of the
 Manager container's own self-monitoring placeholder.
